Hey Vaultscapes,
Lior here, founder of AlphaSignal.
Got some big news.
As you may feel, we're in the middle of the biggest technological shift of =
our generation. New models, breakthroughs, and tools change what's possible=
 almost every day.
But keeping up with it all has become nearly impossible.
In 2025 alone,
280,000 papers
hit arXiv. Add new models, repos, and a constant stream of announcements, a=
nd staying up to date with AI has become a full-time job.
Except you already have one.
And the information is scattered everywhere. Important breakthroughs get bu=
ried, engineers rebuild things that already exist, and nobody knows what th=
ey're missing.
I know the feeling.
Back in 2020, while working at an AI research lab, I was struggling to keep=
 up with research papers myself.
So I started AlphaSignal, a small newsletter to stay up to date with AI.
Then AI exploded, we grew to 350,000 readers, and became the morning read e=
very dev relies on.
But over the years, you kept asking us for three things:
1.
Personalization:
I want only what's relevant to me.
2.
Speed:
I want to know what's happening right now.
3.
Depth:
I want to go beyond the headlines.
So we spent months building something new, and even dropped out of YC to fo=
cus on it.
Meet the new AlphaSignal.
The front page of AI. Personalized for you.
One place for everything happening in AI. We track over 150 AI companies in=
 real time, alongside new papers, models, open-source projects, and announc=
ements, all ranked by relevance and personalized around what you care about=
.
Last week alone, we tracked 1,725 AI announcements.
Here's what you can do:
=E2=86=92
