<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">Lior here, founder of AlphaSignal.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">Got some big news.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">As you may feel, we're in the middle of the=
 biggest technological shift of our generation. New models, breakthroughs, =
and tools change what's possible almost every day.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">But keeping up with it all has become nearl=
y impossible.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">In 2025 alone, <u>280,000 papers</u> hit ar=
Xiv. Add new models, repos, and a constant stream of announcements, and sta=
ying up to date with AI has become a full-time job.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">Except you already have one.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">And the information is scattered everywhere=
. Important breakthroughs get buried, engineers rebuild things that already=
 exist, and nobody knows what they're missing.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">I know the feeling.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">Back in 2020, while working at an AI resear=
ch lab, I was struggling to keep up with research papers myself.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">So I started AlphaSignal, a small newslette=
r to stay up to date with AI.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">Then AI exploded, we grew to 350,000 reader=
s, and became the morning read every dev relies on.</p>
<p style=3D"margin:0 0 16px 0;">But over the years, you kept asking us for =
three things:</p>
